# KEYS.asc — signing keys for sebastienrousseau/dotfiles
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 OR MIT
# Copyright (c) 2015-2026 Sebastien Rousseau
#
# This project signs commits and tags with an **SSH ed25519 key**, not
# GPG. The file is named KEYS.asc because that is the name tooling and
# auditors look for; its contents are in git's `allowed_signers` format
# (ssh-keygen -Y), which is what `gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile` consumes.
#
# A separate GPG key exists for *encrypted vulnerability reports only*
# and never signs releases — see SECURITY.md and
# docs/security/KEY_ROTATION.md. Do not confuse the two.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Verify a release tag against this file
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   git clone https://github.com/sebastienrousseau/dotfiles
#   cd dotfiles
#   git config gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile KEYS.asc
#   git tag -v v0.2.519
#
# Expected output ends with:
#
#   Good "git" signature for sebastian.rousseau@gmail.com
#     with ED25519 key SHA256:f6FG+guRNtT3R36oQFS4oWCx1d10nm+BoaIL3Tkh1r4
#
# Verify a commit the same way:
#
#   git config gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile KEYS.asc
#   git log --show-signature -1
#
# The `git config` above is repo-local. To verify without touching your
# config at all:
#
#   git -c gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile=KEYS.asc tag -v v0.2.519
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cross-check the fingerprint out of band
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A key file in the repository proves nothing on its own — an attacker
# who can rewrite the repo can rewrite this file. Cross-check the
# fingerprint against at least one independent source:
#
#   * GitHub's signing-key API (served by GitHub, not by this repo):
#       curl -s https://api.github.com/users/sebastienrousseau/ssh_signing_keys
#   * The "Verified" badge GitHub shows on tags and commits, which is
#       computed from that same set.
#   * ssh-keygen -lf <(awk 'END{print $3, $4}' KEYS.asc)
#       # KEYS.asc is allowed_signers format, not a bare .pub file, so
#       # feed ssh-keygen just the key fields. Prints the fingerprint below.
#
# Fingerprint (SHA256, ed25519):
#   SHA256:f6FG+guRNtT3R36oQFS4oWCx1d10nm+BoaIL3Tkh1r4
#
# Release artefacts carry their own, stronger provenance — sigstore
# keyless signatures and SLSA attestations produced by CI, not by this
# key. See pkg/VERIFY.md and docs/security/VERIFY_RELEASE.md.
#
# Key rotation policy and history: docs/security/KEY_ROTATION.md
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Allowed signers (ssh-keygen -Y / git allowed_signers format)
# principal(s) [namespaces=...] keytype base64-key
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
sebastian.rousseau@gmail.com namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIDjGRQyeM79nAb4GHcpGzXMKq7HE3xyEOev4gVsnBN1e sebastian.rousseau@gmail.com
